        "title": "refactor(packages): trim private aggregate roots",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThree private workspace packages still exposed aggregate entrypoints that have no consumers. Those roots widened internal package contracts and generated redundant build artifacts even though every live caller already uses focused subpaths.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRemove the unused `@openclaw/memory-host-sdk/runtime`, `@openclaw/web-content-core`, and `@openclaw/media-understanding-common` aggregate surfaces while preserving all focused subpath exports. The matching source barrels, manifest entries, build inputs, TypeScript aliases, and boundary expectation are removed together.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior changes. Internal package surfaces are smaller and package builds no longer emit unused root artifacts.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Code-graph audit plus exhaustive repository import search found zero consumers of the three removed entrypoints.\n- Testbox `tbx_01kxc9pgd9hpar30b6ck9xfg31`:\n  - `pnpm test:serial packages/web-content-core/src/provider-runtime-shared.test.ts packages/media-understanding-common/src/format.test.ts src/plugins/contracts/extension-package-project-boundaries.test.ts test/scripts/tsdown-build.test.ts` (62 tests passed)\n  - `pnpm --filter @openclaw/web-content-core build`\n  - `pnpm --filter @openclaw/media-understanding-common build`\n  - `pnpm build`\n  - `pnpm check:changed -- <9 touched paths>` (full typecheck, core/extension/script lint, and import-cycle checks passed)\n- Fresh `gpt-5.6-sol` medium autoreview:\n  - dirty diff: clean, 0.92 confidence\n  - committed branch: clean, 0.96 confidence\n- `git diff --check`\n",
